  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Everyone plans a retirement age. But the age people actually retire often isn't the one they chose. Here's the real number.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "bank",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "clock"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "When people",
            "really retire."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Surveys say people plan to work into their late sixties. Reality pulls it earlier.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "bank",
          "kicker": "plan vs reality",
          "line": "Earlier than planned",
          "sub": "life gets a vote"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The real retirement age is frequently forced, not chosen.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-retage",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · retirement age"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The actual median retirement age lands around sixty-two, not sixty-seven.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "~62",
          "label": "the real median retirement age",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Why earlier? Layoffs, health problems, and caring for family all strike before the plan.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "Forced out early",
          "props": [
            "x",
            "clock"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Sixty-two is also the earliest you can claim Social Security.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-ss",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · Social Security"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The lesson is blunt. You might have fewer working years than you're counting on.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "fewer years",
          "label": "than you think",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And Medicare doesn't even start until sixty-five.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-medicare",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · Medicare"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Plan for sixty-seven, but quietly prepare to be done by sixty-two.",
